\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The training domain in three coordinate systems, all built from the same $109\,460$ training-trajectory snapshots of this RVE. Left: the first three raw POD coordinates $(q_{{\rm  tot},1},q_{{\rm  tot},2},q_{{\rm  tot},3})$, a curved, self-intersecting ribbon that is POD-optimal for reconstruction but not well suited to regression. Middle: the same snapshots in the structured, least-squares-fitted primary coordinates $\bm  {q}$ actually used as~\eqref  {eq:decoder}'s input, recovering a near-affine, boustrophedon sweep. Right: the macro-strain domain itself, $\bm  {\varepsilon }=(E_{11},E_{22},\gamma _{12})$, for comparison. The middle and right panels are visually close by construction: that closeness is exactly the least-squares fit being verified, not assumed.}}{22}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
